/-!
# The positivity of the intersection multiplicity on a nonsingular variety

Let `X` be a nonsingular variety over an algebraically closed field `k` — the chapter's own
convention, Tag 0AZ8 — let `V`, `W ⊆ X` be closed subschemes which intersect properly along an
irreducible component `Z` of `V ∩ W`, and let `ξ` be the generic point of `Z`. Then
`e(X, V · W, Z) > 0`. That is Stacks tag 0B0V, one of the main results of Serre's *Algèbre
locale*, and it is
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.intersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegular` below.

## The assembly

Present `V` and `W` by closed immersions `ι_V : V ⟶ X`, `ι_W : W ⟶ X` and let `ζ` be a point of
the scheme-theoretic intersection `V ×_X W`, with images `v` in `V`, `w` in `W` and `ξ` in `X`.
Write `A = 𝒪_{X, ξ}`, `I`, `J` for the local ideals of `V`, `W` at `ξ`,
`B = 𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}` and `R = 𝒪_{Spec k, f ξ}` — which is a field, so that no comparison of
`R` with `k` is needed anywhere.

The local ring `B` is a localization of `A ⊗_R A` through a map `φ` admitting a retraction
`d : B → A` of the multiplication map, and `φ ∘ includeLeft`, `φ ∘ includeRight` are the local
ring maps of the two projections: that is
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.diagonal_stalk_isLocalization`. The pair on `B` is `(I_Δ, J')`
with `I_Δ = ker d` the ideal of the diagonal and `J'` the stalk at `Δ(ξ)` of the ideal sheaf
`pr₁^{-1} ℐ_V ⊔ pr₂^{-1} ℐ_W` cutting out `V ×ₖ W`, which is the ideal `φ(prodIdeal I J) B`
generated by the image of the ideal of `V × W`
(`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.stalk_sup_comap_diagonal_eq`). Five clauses are needed, and
`Stacks.Intersection.localIntersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegularSequence` — the
Hilbert-polynomial formula of Stacks tag 0B04 — then closes the tag:

1. `I_Δ` is generated by a regular family `g : Fin c → B` with `c = dim X`, and
2. that family is a regular sequence — both are
   `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.exists_isRegular_fin_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal`
   (Stacks tag 0B0Q);
3. `dim (B ⧸ (I_Δ ⊔ J')) = dim (A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)) = 0`, which is
   `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_stalkMap_diagonal` below, the
   geometric form of `ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_map_prodIdeal`;
4. `dim B ≤ dim (B ⧸ I_Δ) + dim (B ⧸ J')`, the properness inequality for the diagonal pair,
   which is `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_stalk_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal`
   below;
5. `(I_Δ).localIntersectionMultiplicity (B ⧸ J') = I.localIntersectionMultiplicity (A ⧸ J)`,
   the equality of multiplicities of Stacks tag 0B0U read at the one point `Δ(ξ)`, which is
   `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.localIntersectionMultiplicity_stalk_comap_diagonal_eq`.

Finally `B` is a regular local ring: an algebraically closed field is perfect, so `X ×ₖ X` is
smooth over `k` as soon as `X` is regular
(`AlgebraicGeometry.smooth_pullback_of_isRegular`), and the local rings of a scheme smooth over
a field are regular.

## Clause 4 needs only an inclusion, not an identification

The properness clause is an *inequality*, so it needs only the inclusion `J' ≤ ker ρ`, where
`ρ : B → 𝒪_{V ×ₖ W, p}` is the local ring map of the closed immersion `V ×ₖ W ⟶ X ×ₖ X` read at
the point `p = interToProd ζ` of `V ×ₖ W` lying over `Δ(ξ)`. That inclusion is elementary: by
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.prodMap_comp_fst` the composite `ρ ∘ φ ∘ includeLeft` factors
through `ι_V.stalkMap v`, whose kernel is `I`, and symmetrically through
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.prodMap_comp_snd` on the right; the reduction of the inclusion to
those two factorizations is `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.map_prodIdeal_le_ker` below, and the
transports the two factorizations need are the `stalkMap` lemmas below. The inclusion gives a
surjection `B ⧸ J' ↠ 𝒪_{V ×ₖ W, p}`, hence `dim 𝒪_{V ×ₖ W, p} ≤ dim (B ⧸ J')`, which is the
favourable direction; with
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_stalk_prod_add_ringKrullDim_stalk` and
`ringKrullDim_stalk_pullback_diagonal` that yields clause 4 with no cancellation, since
`dim B = dim X + dim A`, `dim (B ⧸ I_Δ) = dim A` and
`dim A + dim X ≤ dim 𝒪_{V, v} + dim 𝒪_{W, w} + dim X = dim 𝒪_{V ×ₖ W, p} + dim A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.intersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegular` — **Stacks tag
  0B0V**, the positivity of `e(X, V · W, Z)`.
* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_stalk_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal` and
  `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_stalkMap_diagonal` — clauses 4
  and 3 of the assembly above, the two numerical conditions satisfied by the diagonal pair.
* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.quotProdIdealEquiv` — the algebraic identification
  `(A ⊗_R A) ⧸ prodIdeal I J ≅ (A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J)`, with
  `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.extQuotIso` its form in `ModuleCat (A ⊗_R A)` for the exterior
  action, and `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.quotMapProdIdealIso` the resulting identification
  of `B ⧸ φ(prodIdeal I J) B` with the base change of `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J)` to `B`.
* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.map_prodIdeal_le_ker` — the image of the ideal of `V × W` lies
  in the kernel of a ring map killing `I` on the left and `J` on the right.
* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.stalkMap_comp_eq_of_comm` — the local ring maps of a
  commutative square of schemes agree up to the transport along the equality of points, and
  `stalkMap_congr_eqToHom`, `stalkMap_eq_eqToHom_comp`,
  `map_eqToHom_idealSheafData_stalk`, `surjective_eqToHom_hom` the transports that go with it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Proposition 43.20.1 (Tag 0B0V)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B0U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B0T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B0Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B04](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B04)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B1I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B1I)
* [Serre, *Algèbre locale. Multiplicités*][Serre_algebre_locale]
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal

/-! ### The quotient of `A ⊗_R A` by the ideal of `V × W` -/

section Algebra

variable {R A : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]

/-- The map `(A ⊗_R A) ⧸ prodIdeal I J → (A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J)` induced by the two quotient
maps. -/
noncomputable def quotProdIdealHom (I J : Ideal A) :
    ((A ⊗[R] A) ⧸ prodIdeal (R := R) I J) →ₐ[R] (A ⧸ I) ⊗[R] (A ⧸ J) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J))
    (by
      intro a ha
      refine (?_ : prodIdeal (R := R) I J ≤ RingHom.ker
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J)).toRingHom) ha
      refine sup_le ?_ ?_
      · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
        intro x hx
        simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
        change Algebra.TensorProduct.map _ _ (x ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) = 0
        rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul]
        simp [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 hx]
      · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
        intro x hx
        simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
        change Algebra.TensorProduct.map _ _ ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] x) = 0
        rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul]
        simp [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 hx])

/-- The map `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J) → (A ⊗_R A) ⧸ prodIdeal I J` inverse to
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.quotProdIdealHom`: both inclusions land in the quotient because
the ideal of `V × W` contains the images of `I` and of `J`. -/
noncomputable def prodIdealQuotHom (I J : Ideal A) :
    ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[R] (A ⧸ J)) →ₐ[R] ((A ⊗[R] A) ⧸ prodIdeal (R := R) I J) :=
  Algebra.TensorProduct.lift
    (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ I
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)).comp
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft)
      (by
        intro a ha
        change Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) = 0
        exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2
          (Submodule.mem_sup_left (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha))))
    (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ J
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)).comp
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight)
      (by
        intro a ha
        change Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] a) = 0
        exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2
          (Submodule.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha))))
    (fun _ _ => .all _ _)

/-- `quotProdIdealHom I J` sends the class of `x` to its image under the tensor product of the
two quotient maps. -/
theorem quotProdIdealHom_mk (I J : Ideal A) (x : A ⊗[R] A) :
    quotProdIdealHom (R := R) I J (Ideal.Quotient.mk (prodIdeal (R := R) I J) x) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.map (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J) x := rfl

/-- `prodIdealQuotHom I J` sends `ā ⊗ b̄` to the class of `a ⊗ b`. -/
theorem prodIdealQuotHom_tmul (I J : Ideal A) (a b : A) :
    prodIdealQuotHom (R := R) I J (Ideal.Quotient.mk I a ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk J b) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (prodIdeal (R := R) I J) (a ⊗ₜ[R] b) := by
  rw [prodIdealQuotHom, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul]
  show Ideal.Quotient.mk (prodIdeal (R := R) I J) (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) *
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (prodIdeal (R := R) I J) ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] b) = _
  rw [← map_mul, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul]

/-- **The quotient of `A ⊗_R A` by the ideal of `V × W`.** For two ideals `I`, `J` of an
`R`-algebra `A` the quotient of `A ⊗_R A` by `prodIdeal I J` is `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J)`. -/
noncomputable def quotProdIdealEquiv (I J : Ideal A) :
    ((A ⊗[R] A) ⧸ prodIdeal (R := R) I J) ≃ₐ[R] (A ⧸ I) ⊗[R] (A ⧸ J) :=
  AlgEquiv.ofAlgHom (quotProdIdealHom I J) (prodIdealQuotHom I J)
    (by
      refine AlgHom.ext fun x => ?_
      induction x with
      | zero => simp
      | add u v hu hv => simp only [map_add, hu, hv, AlgHom.id_apply]
      | tmul u v =>
          obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective u
          obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective v
          rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, prodIdealQuotHom_tmul, quotProdIdealHom_mk, AlgHom.id_apply,
            Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul]
          rfl)
    (by
      refine AlgHom.ext fun x => ?_
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
      induction y with
      | zero => simp
      | add u v hu hv =>
          rw [map_add] at *
          simp only [map_add, hu, hv, AlgHom.id_apply]
      | tmul a b =>
          rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, quotProdIdealHom_mk, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul,
            AlgHom.id_apply]
          exact prodIdealQuotHom_tmul I J a b)

/-- The forward map of `quotProdIdealEquiv I J` is `quotProdIdealHom I J`. -/
theorem quotProdIdealEquiv_apply (I J : Ideal A) (x : (A ⊗[R] A) ⧸ prodIdeal (R := R) I J) :
    quotProdIdealEquiv (R := R) I J x = quotProdIdealHom I J x := rfl

attribute [local instance] exteriorModule

/-- The exterior action of `A ⊗_R A` on `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_R (A ⧸ J)` is multiplication by the image
under the two quotient maps: the exterior action and the ring structure agree. -/
theorem exteriorModule_smul_eq_mul_prodIdeal (I J : Ideal A) (r : A ⊗[R] A)
    (y : (A ⧸ I) ⊗[R] (A ⧸ J)) :
    r • y =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.map (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J) r * y := by
  induction r with
  | zero => simp
  | add r s hr hs => rw [add_smul, hr, hs, map_add, add_mul]
  | tmul a b =>
      induction y with
      | zero => simp
      | add u v hu hv => rw [smul_add, hu, hv, mul_add]
      | tmul u v =>
          obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective u
          obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective v
          rw [exteriorModule_smul_tmul, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul,
            Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul]
          rfl

end Algebra

section AlgebraField

variable {k A : Type u} [Field k] [CommRing A] [Algebra k A]

attribute [local instance] exteriorModule

/-- `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.quotProdIdealEquiv` read in `ModuleCat (A ⊗[k] A)`: the
quotient of `A ⊗[k] A` by the ideal of `V × W` is the exterior tensor product of the two
quotients. -/
noncomputable def extQuotIso (I J : Ideal A) :
    ModuleCat.of (A ⊗[k] A) ((A ⊗[k] A) ⧸ prodIdeal (R := k) I J) ≅
      extObj (k := k) (A ⧸ I) (A ⧸ J) :=
  LinearEquiv.toModuleIso
    (AddEquiv.toLinearEquiv (quotProdIdealEquiv (R := k) I J).toAddEquiv (by
      intro c x
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
      change quotProdIdealEquiv (R := k) I J (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (c * y)) = _
      rw [quotProdIdealEquiv_apply, quotProdIdealHom_mk, exteriorModule_smul_eq_mul_prodIdeal,
        map_mul]
      rfl))

/-- **The ideal of `V × W` in a localization of `A ⊗[k] A`.** For a ring map
`φ : A ⊗[k] A → B` the quotient of `B` by the ideal generated by the image of
`prodIdeal I J` is the base change to `B` of the exterior tensor product
`(A ⧸ I) ⊗[k] (A ⧸ J)`.

For `B = 𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}` this says that the local ring of `V ×ₖ W` cut out inside `B` by the
ideal `J'` generated by the ideal of `V × W` is the base change of `𝒪_{V, v} ⊗ 𝒪_{W, w}`, which
is the second module the reduction to the diagonal feeds to `diagonalTorLocalizedIso`. -/
noncomputable def quotMapProdIdealIso {B : Type u} [CommRing B] (φ : (A ⊗[k] A) →+* B)
    (I J : Ideal A) :
    ModuleCat.of B (B ⧸ Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := k) I J)) ≅
      (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj (extObj (k := k) (A ⧸ I) (A ⧸ J)) :=
  letI := φ.toAlgebra
  LinearEquiv.toModuleIso
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot B
        (prodIdeal (R := k) I J)).toLinearEquiv ≪≫
    (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).mapIso (extQuotIso I J)

end AlgebraField

/-! ### The ideal of `V × W` lies in the kernel of the local ring map of `V ×ₖ W` -/

section Pure

variable {R A B C : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]

/-- The image of the ideal of `V × W` lies in the kernel of a ring map which kills `I` through
the left inclusion and `J` through the right one. -/
theorem map_prodIdeal_le_ker (φ : (A ⊗[R] A) →+* B) (ρ : B →+* C) (I J : Ideal A)
    (hI : I ≤ RingHom.ker ((ρ.comp φ).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom))
    (hJ : J ≤ RingHom.ker ((ρ.comp φ).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : A →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] A).toRingHom)) :
    Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := R) I J) ≤ RingHom.ker ρ := by
  rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  exact sup_le (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 hI) (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 hJ)

/-- Quotienting a ring by the kernel of a surjection does not change the Krull dimension. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_eq {ρ : B →+* C} (hρ : Function.Surjective ρ) :
    ringKrullDim (B ⧸ RingHom.ker ρ) = ringKrullDim C :=
  ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hρ)

/-- **Clause 4 of the 0B0V assembly: the properness inequality for the diagonal pair.** Let
`φ : A ⊗_R A → B` admit a surjective retraction `d : B → A` of the multiplication map, and let
`ρ : B → C` be a surjective ring map whose kernel contains the image of `I` under `φ ∘
includeLeft` and of `J` under `φ ∘ includeRight`. If `dim B = n + dim A`,
`dim C + dim A = dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J) + n` and `dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)`, then
`dim B ≤ dim (B ⧸ ker d) + dim (B ⧸ φ(prodIdeal I J) B)`.

For `B = 𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}`, `C = 𝒪_{V ×ₖ W, p}`, `d` the local ring map of the diagonal, `ρ` the
local ring map of the closed immersion `V ×ₖ W ⟶ X ×ₖ X` and `n = dim X`, this is clause 4 of
the reduction to the diagonal: no cancellation is needed, since the chain
`dim B = dim A + dim X ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J) + dim X = dim C + dim A
  ≤ dim (B ⧸ φ(prodIdeal I J) B) + dim (B ⧸ ker d)`
goes through using only the hypothesis `dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)` and the favourable
direction `dim C ≤ dim (B ⧸ φ(prodIdeal I J) B)` of `map_prodIdeal_le_ker`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal (φ : (A ⊗[R] A) →+* B) (d : B →+* A)
    (ρ : B →+* C) (hd : (Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A)).toRingHom = d.comp φ)
    (hdsurj : Function.Surjective d) (hρsurj : Function.Surjective ρ) (I J : Ideal A)
    (hI : I ≤ RingHom.ker ((ρ.comp φ).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom))
    (hJ : J ≤ RingHom.ker ((ρ.comp φ).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : A →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] A).toRingHom))
    {n : WithBot ℕ∞} (hdimB : ringKrullDim B = n + ringKrullDim A)
    (hdimC : ringKrullDim C + ringKrullDim A =
      ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J) + n)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim A ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) :
    ringKrullDim B ≤ ringKrullDim (B ⧸ RingHom.ker d) +
      ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)) := by
  have hJ' := map_prodIdeal_le_ker φ ρ I J hI hJ
  have hCle : ringKrullDim C ≤ ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)) := by
    rw [← ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_eq hρsurj]
    exact ringKrullDim_le_of_surjective _ (Ideal.Quotient.factor_surjective hJ')
  calc ringKrullDim B = ringKrullDim A + n := by rw [hdimB, add_comm]
    _ ≤ (ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I) + ringKrullDim (A ⧸ J)) + n := by gcongr
    _ = ringKrullDim C + ringKrullDim A := by rw [← hdimC]
    _ ≤ ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)) + ringKrullDim A := by gcongr
    _ = ringKrullDim (B ⧸ RingHom.ker d) +
          ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (R := R) I J)) := by
      rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_eq hdsurj, add_comm]

end Pure

/-! ### Transport of local ring maps along equalities of points -/

section Transport

/-- A transport of local ring maps along an equality of morphisms. -/
theorem stalkMap_congr_eqToHom {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} {a b : Z ⟶ Y} (h : a = b) (z : Z) :
    a.stalkMap z =
      eqToHom (congrArg Y.presheaf.stalk (congrArg (fun n : Z ⟶ Y => n z) h)) ≫
        b.stalkMap z := by
  subst h; simp

/-- A transport of local ring maps along an equality of points. -/
theorem stalkMap_eq_eqToHom_comp {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ Y) {z z' : Z} (h : z = z') :
    g.stalkMap z =
      eqToHom (congrArg Y.presheaf.stalk (congrArg (fun t : Z => g t) h)) ≫
        g.stalkMap z' ≫ eqToHom (congrArg Z.presheaf.stalk h.symm) := by
  subst h; simp

/-- For a commutative square `m ≫ p = q ≫ i` the local ring map of `p` followed by that of `m`
is the local ring map of `i` followed by that of `q`, up to the transport along the resulting
equality of points. -/
theorem stalkMap_comp_eq_of_comm {Q P X' V' : Scheme.{u}} (m : Q ⟶ P) (p : P ⟶ X')
    (q : Q ⟶ V') (i : V' ⟶ X') (hcomm : m ≫ p = q ≫ i) (pt : Q) :
    p.stalkMap (m pt) ≫ m.stalkMap pt =
      eqToHom (congrArg X'.presheaf.stalk
          (congrArg (fun n : Q ⟶ X' => n pt) hcomm)) ≫
        i.stalkMap (q pt) ≫ q.stalkMap pt := by
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp, stalkMap_congr_eqToHom hcomm pt, Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]
  rfl

/-- A transport along an equality of points carries the stalk of an ideal sheaf to the stalk at
the other point. -/
theorem map_eqToHom_idealSheafData_stalk {X : Scheme.{u}} (S : X.IdealSheafData) {x y : X}
    (h : x = y) :
    Ideal.map (eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk h)).hom
        (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk S x) =
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk S y := by
  subst h
  simp [Ideal.map_id]

/-- A transport along an equality of rings is surjective. -/
theorem surjective_eqToHom_hom {R S : CommRingCat.{u}} (h : R = S) :
    Function.Surjective (eqToHom h).hom := by
  subst h
  rw [eqToHom_refl]
  exact fun x => ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- The two images in `X` of a point of the fibre product `V ×_X W` agree. -/
theorem image_eq_of_mem_pullback {X V W : Scheme.{u}} (iV : V ⟶ X) (iW : W ⟶ X)
    (ζ : ↑(pullback iV iW)) :
    iW (pullback.snd iV iW ζ) = iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ) := by
  have := congrArg (fun n : (pullback iV iW : Scheme.{u}) ⟶ X => n ζ)
    (pullback.condition (f := iV) (g := iW))
  simpa using this.symm

/-- A transport along an equality of rings followed by a surjection is surjective. -/
private theorem surjective_eqToHom_comp_hom {R S T : CommRingCat.{u}} (h : R = S) {g : S ⟶ T}
    (hg : Function.Surjective g.hom) : Function.Surjective (eqToHom h ≫ g).hom := by
  simpa [CommRingCat.hom_comp] using hg.comp (surjective_eqToHom_hom h)

/-- For a commutative square `m ≫ p = q ≫ i`, an element killed by the local ring map of `i` is
killed by `p`'s local ring map followed by `m`'s, up to transports along the equalities of
points. -/
private theorem ker_stalkMap_le_ker_comp {X' V' P Q : Scheme.{u}} {T : Type*} [CommRing T]
    (m : Q ⟶ P) (p : P ⟶ X') (q : Q ⟶ V') (i : V' ⟶ X') (hcomm : m ≫ p = q ≫ i) (pt : Q)
    {Δξ : P} {ξ : X'} {v : V'} (hmpt : m pt = Δξ) (hqv : q pt = v) (hξ : i v = ξ)
    (hpξ : p Δξ = ξ) (φ : T →+* P.presheaf.stalk Δξ) (F : X'.presheaf.stalk ξ →+* T)
    (hF : φ.comp F =
      (p.stalkMap Δξ).hom.comp (eqToHom (congrArg X'.presheaf.stalk hpξ.symm)).hom) :
    RingHom.ker (eqToHom (congrArg X'.presheaf.stalk hξ.symm) ≫ i.stalkMap v).hom ≤
      RingHom.ker (((eqToHom (congrArg P.presheaf.stalk hmpt.symm) ≫ m.stalkMap pt).hom.comp
        φ).comp F) := by
  subst hmpt hqv hξ
  intro a ha
  have e : p.stalkMap (m pt) ≫ m.stalkMap pt =
      eqToHom (congrArg X'.presheaf.stalk hpξ) ≫ i.stalkMap (q pt) ≫ q.stalkMap pt :=
    stalkMap_comp_eq_of_comm m p q i hcomm pt
  have key : (eqToHom (congrArg X'.presheaf.stalk hpξ.symm) ≫ p.stalkMap (m pt) ≫
      m.stalkMap pt) = i.stalkMap (q pt) ≫ q.stalkMap pt := by
    rw [e]; simp only [eqToHom_trans_assoc, eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp]
  simp only [RingHom.mem_ker, CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply, eqToHom_refl,
    CommRingCat.hom_id, RingHom.id_apply] at ha ⊢
  have h2 := congrArg (fun g => g.hom a) key
  simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply] at h2
  rw [← RingHom.comp_apply φ F, hF, RingHom.comp_apply, h2, ha, map_zero]

end Transport

/-! ### Clause 4 of the 0B0V assembly, geometric form -/

section Geometric

open scoped TensorProduct

/-- **Clause 4 of the 0B0V assembly.** Let `X` be a variety over a field `k`, let
`ι_V : V ⟶ X`, `ι_W : W ⟶ X` be closed immersions and let `ζ` be a point of the
scheme-theoretic intersection `V ×_X W`, with images `v` in `V`, `w` in `W` and `ξ` in `X`. If
`dim 𝒪_{X,ξ} ≤ dim 𝒪_{V,v} + dim 𝒪_{W,w}`, then, for `B = 𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}`,

`dim B ≤ dim (B ⧸ I_Δ) + dim (B ⧸ J')`,

with `I_Δ` the kernel of the local ring map of the diagonal and `J'` the stalk at `Δ(ξ)` of the
ideal sheaf `pr₁^* ℐ_V ⊔ pr₂^* ℐ_W` of `X ×ₖ X` which cuts out `V ×ₖ W`. This is the properness
inequality for the diagonal pair `(Δ, V ×ₖ W)` on `X ×ₖ X`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X V W : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] (iV : V ⟶ X) (iW : W ⟶ X)
    [IsClosedImmersion iV] [IsClosedImmersion iW] (ζ : ↑(pullback iV iW))
    (hproper : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))) ≤
      ringKrullDim (V.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)) +
        ringKrullDim (W.presheaf.stalk (pullback.snd iV iW ζ))) :
    ringKrullDim ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk
        (pullback.diagonal f (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)))) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk
          (pullback.diagonal f (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))) ⧸
        RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap
          (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))).hom) +
      ringKrullDim ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk
          (pullback.diagonal f (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))) ⧸
        AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
          (iV.ker.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ iW.ker.comap (pullback.snd f f))
          (pullback.diagonal f (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)))) := by
  set v : V := pullback.fst iV iW ζ with hv
  set w : W := pullback.snd iV iW ζ with hw
  set ξ : X := iV v with hξ
  set P := (pullback f f : Scheme.{u}) with hP
  set Q := (pullback (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f) : Scheme.{u}) with hQ
  set pt : Q := interToProd f iV iW ζ with hpt
  set m : Q ⟶ P := prodMap f iV iW with hm
  set Δξ : P := pullback.diagonal f ξ with hΔξ
  have hwξ : iW w = ξ := image_eq_of_mem_pullback iV iW ζ
  have hfst : pullback.fst f f Δξ = ξ := by
    rw [hΔξ, ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, pullback.diagonal_fst]; rfl
  have hsnd : pullback.snd f f Δξ = ξ := by
    rw [hΔξ, ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, pullback.diagonal_snd]; rfl
  let := (f.stalkMap ξ).hom.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨φ, hφleft0, hφright0, hφd, M, hM⟩ := diagonal_stalk_isLocalization f ξ
  have hφleft : φ.comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom =
      ((pullback.fst f f).stalkMap Δξ).hom.comp
        (eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hfst.symm)).hom := by
    rw [hφleft0, CommRingCat.hom_comp]
  have hφright : φ.comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom =
      ((pullback.snd f f).stalkMap Δξ).hom.comp
        (eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hsnd.symm)).hom := by
    rw [hφright0, CommRingCat.hom_comp]
  set d : (pullback f f).presheaf.stalk Δξ →+* X.presheaf.stalk ξ :=
    ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom with hdDef
  have hd : (Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' _ (S := X.presheaf.stalk ξ)).toRingHom = d.comp φ :=
    hφd.symm
  have hdsurj : Function.Surjective d := (pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap_surjective ξ
  have hptfst : pullback.fst (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f) pt = v := by
    rw [hpt, hv, ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, interToProd_comp_fst]
  have hptsnd : pullback.snd (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f) pt = w := by
    rw [hpt, hw, ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, interToProd_comp_snd]
  have hmpt : m pt = Δξ := by
    have := prodMap_interToProd_apply f iV iW ζ
    simpa [hpt, hm, hξ, hv, hΔξ] using this
  set ρCat : (pullback f f).presheaf.stalk Δξ ⟶
      (pullback (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f)).presheaf.stalk pt :=
    eqToHom (congrArg (pullback f f).presheaf.stalk hmpt.symm) ≫ m.stalkMap pt with hρDef
  have hρsurj : Function.Surjective ρCat.hom :=
    surjective_eqToHom_comp_hom _ ((prodMap f iV iW).stalkMap_surjective pt)
  have hI : RingHom.ker (iV.stalkMap v).hom ≤
      RingHom.ker ((ρCat.hom.comp φ).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom) :=
    ker_stalkMap_le_ker_comp m (pullback.fst f f) (pullback.fst (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f)) iV
      (prodMap_comp_fst f iV iW) pt hmpt hptfst rfl hfst φ _ hφleft
  have hJ : RingHom.ker ((eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hwξ.symm) ≫
        iW.stalkMap w).hom) ≤
      RingHom.ker ((ρCat.hom.comp φ).comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : X.presheaf.stalk ξ →ₐ[_]
          X.presheaf.stalk ξ ⊗[_] X.presheaf.stalk ξ).toRingHom) :=
    ker_stalkMap_le_ker_comp m (pullback.snd f f) (pullback.snd (iV ≫ f) (iW ≫ f)) iW
      (prodMap_comp_snd f iV iW) pt hmpt hptsnd hwξ hsnd φ _ hφright
  have hIeq := ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_eq (iV.stalkMap_surjective v)
  have hJeq := ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_eq
    (surjective_eqToHom_comp_hom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hwξ.symm) (iW.stalkMap_surjective w))
  -- the local ideal of `V ×ₖ W` at `Δ(ξ)`, read through the presentation `φ`
  have hIst : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk iV.ker ξ =
      RingHom.ker (iV.stalkMap v).hom :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_ker_of_isClosedImmersion iV v
  have hJst : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk iW.ker ξ =
      RingHom.ker ((eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hwξ.symm) ≫ iW.stalkMap w).hom) := by
    have key : ∀ (y : X) (h : iW w = y),
        AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk iW.ker y =
          RingHom.ker ((eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk h.symm) ≫ iW.stalkMap w).hom) := by
      intro y h
      subst h
      simpa using AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_ker_of_isClosedImmersion iW w
    exact key ξ hwξ
  have hstalkeq : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (iV.ker.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ iW.ker.comap (pullback.snd f f)) Δξ =
      Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (RingHom.ker (iV.stalkMap v).hom)
        (RingHom.ker ((eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hwξ.symm) ≫
          iW.stalkMap w).hom))) := by
    rw [prodIdeal, Ideal.map_sup, Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, hφleft, hφright,
      ← hIst, ← hJst]
    exact stalk_sup_comap_diagonal_eq f iV.ker iW.ker ξ
  rw [hstalkeq]
  refine ringKrullDim_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal φ d ρCat.hom hd hdsurj hρsurj
    (RingHom.ker (iV.stalkMap v).hom)
    (RingHom.ker ((eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk hwξ.symm) ≫ iW.stalkMap w).hom))
    hI hJ (n := topologicalKrullDim X) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · exact ringKrullDim_stalk_pullback_diagonal f ξ
  · rw [hIeq, hJeq, hpt, hξ, hv, hw]
    exact ringKrullDim_stalk_prod_add_ringKrullDim_stalk f iV iW ζ
  · rwa [hIeq, hJeq]

/-! ### Clause 3 of the 0B0V assembly, geometric form -/

/-- **Clause 3 of the 0B0V assembly.** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes, `x` a point of
`X` and `I`, `J` two quasi-coherent sheaves of ideals on `X`, cutting out closed subschemes `V`,
`W`. Then the quotient of `B = 𝒪_{X ×_Y X, Δ(x)}` by the local ideal of the diagonal together
with the local ideal of `V ×_Y W` has the same dimension as the local ring
`𝒪_{X, x} ⧸ (I ⊔ J)_x` of the scheme-theoretic intersection `V ∩ W` at `x`.

Geometrically this is `Δ^{-1}(Δ ∩ V ×_Y W) = V ∩ W`. It transports the statement that `x` is the
generic point of an irreducible component of `V ∩ W`, in the form `dim 𝒪_{V ∩ W, x} = 0`, to the
same statement for the pair `(Δ, V ×_Y W)` at `Δ(x)`; that is the zero-dimensionality hypothesis
of the multiplicity formula for a regular sequence. No hypothesis on `f`, `X`, `Y` or on the two
ideal sheaves is used. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_stalkMap_diagonal {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (I J : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) :
    ringKrullDim ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f x) ⧸
        (RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap x).hom ⊔
          AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
            (I.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ J.comap (pullback.snd f f))
            (pullback.diagonal f x))) =
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸
        AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk (I ⊔ J) x) := by
  let := (f.stalkMap x).hom.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨φ, hleft, hright, hd, M, hM⟩ := diagonal_stalk_isLocalization f x
  have hleft' : φ.comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom =
      ((pullback.fst f f).stalkMap (pullback.diagonal f x)).hom.comp
        (eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk
          (pullback_fst_diagonal_apply f x).symm)).hom := by
    rw [hleft, CommRingCat.hom_comp]
  have hright' : φ.comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom =
      ((pullback.snd f f).stalkMap (pullback.diagonal f x)).hom.comp
        (eqToHom (congrArg X.presheaf.stalk
          (pullback_snd_diagonal_apply f x).symm)).hom := by
    rw [hright, CommRingCat.hom_comp]
  have hstalkeq : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (I.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ J.comap (pullback.snd f f)) (pullback.diagonal f x) =
      Ideal.map φ (prodIdeal (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I x)
        (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk J x)) := by
    rw [prodIdeal, Ideal.map_sup, Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, hleft', hright']
    exact stalk_sup_comap_diagonal_eq f I J x
  rw [hstalkeq, AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_sup]
  exact ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_map_prodIdeal φ
    ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap x).hom hd.symm
    ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap_surjective x) _ _

/-! ### The whole of Stacks 0B0V -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0B0V.** One of the main results of Serre's *Algèbre locale*. Let `X`
be a nonsingular variety over an algebraically closed field `k` — the chapter's convention — let
`V`, `W ⊆ X` be closed subvarieties which intersect properly and let `Z` be an irreducible
component of `V ∩ W`, with generic point `ξ`. Then `e(X, V · W, Z) > 0`.

Here `V` and `W` are presented by closed immersions `ι_V : V ⟶ X`, `ι_W : W ⟶ X`, the
scheme-theoretic intersection `V ∩ W` is the fibre product `V ×_X W`, and `ξ` is the image in
`X` of a point `ζ` of it. The two numerical hypotheses are the source's own, read at `ξ`:
`dim 𝒪_{V ∩ W, ξ} = 0` says that the closure of `ξ` is an irreducible component `Z` of `V ∩ W`,
and `dim 𝒪_{X, ξ} ≤ dim 𝒪_{V, v} + dim 𝒪_{W, w}` says that `V` and `W` intersect properly along
`Z`, which is Tag 0B1I's criterion: by Tag 0A21 the three local dimensions are
`dim X - dim Z`, `dim V - dim Z` and `dim W - dim Z`, so the inequality is exactly
`dim Z ≤ dim V + dim W - dim X`. The multiplicity `e(X, V · W, Z)` is
`Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity` (Tag 0AZR), the alternating sum
`∑ᵢ (-1)ⁱ length 𝒪_{X,ξ} Torᵢ^{𝒪_{X,ξ}}(𝒪_{V,ξ}, 𝒪_{W,ξ})`.

The proof is the source's. The reduction to the diagonal (Tag 0B0U) identifies `e(X, V · W, Z)`
with `e(X ×ₖ X, Δ · V ×ₖ W, Δ(Z))`, by
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.localIntersectionMultiplicity_stalk_comap_diagonal_eq`; the
diagonal of a nonsingular variety is a regular immersion (Tag 0B0Q), so the local ideal of `Δ`
at `Δ(ξ)` is generated by a regular sequence of `dim X` elements
(`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.exists_isRegular_fin_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal`); and for
such a pair the multiplicity is `dim X !` times the positive leading coefficient of a Hilbert
polynomial (Tag 0B04,
`Stacks.Intersection.localIntersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegularSequence`). The two
numerical hypotheses of that last step are supplied for the diagonal pair by clauses 3 and 4
above, and `X ×ₖ X` is regular because `X` is and `k` is perfect. -/
@[stacks 0B0V "the whole proposition, for a nonsingular variety over an algebraically closed \
field — the chapter's own convention, Tag 0AZ8. `V` and `W` are closed subschemes of `X`, \
presented by closed immersions, so the statement proved is more general than the source's, \
which takes them integral; `V ∩ W` is the fibre product `V ×_X W` and `ξ` is the image in `X` \
of a point `ζ` of it. That the closure `Z` of `ξ` is an irreducible component of `V ∩ W` is \
`dim 𝒪_{V ∩ W, ξ} = 0`, and that `V` and `W` intersect properly along `Z` is \
`dim 𝒪_{X, ξ} ≤ dim 𝒪_{V, v} + dim 𝒪_{W, w}`, the criterion of Tag 0B1I — by Tag 0A21 it is \
`dim Z ≤ dim V + dim W - dim X`, so it is implied by, and weaker than, the source's global \
proper intersection. `e(X, V · W, Z)` is `Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity` \
(Tag 0AZR). Everything the proof uses is proved in this development: the reduction to the \
diagonal of Tag 0B0U, the regular sequence cutting out the diagonal of Tag 0B0Q, and the \
Hilbert-polynomial formula of Tag 0B04."]
theorem intersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegular {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X V W : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] (hX : IsRegular X)
    (iV : V ⟶ X) (iW : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion iV] [IsClosedImmersion iW]
    (ζ : ↑(pullback iV iW))
    (hcomponent : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)) ⧸
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk (iV.ker ⊔ iW.ker)
        (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))) = 0)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ))) ≤
      ringKrullDim (V.presheaf.stalk (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)) +
        ringKrullDim (W.presheaf.stalk (pullback.snd iV iW ζ))) :
    0 < Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity iV.ker iW.ker
      (iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ)) := by
  set ξ : X := iV (pullback.fst iV iW ζ) with hξ
  have : Smooth (pullback.fst f f ≫ f) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.smooth_pullback_of_isRegular f f hX hX
  have : IsRegularLocalRing
      ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field
      (pullback.fst f f ≫ f) _
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Stacks.Intersection.exists_topologicalKrullDim_eq_natCast f
  obtain ⟨g, hgreg, hgspan⟩ :=
    exists_isRegular_fin_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal f hX ξ hc
  have h0 : ringKrullDim ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ) ⧸
      (RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom ⊔
        AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
          (iV.ker.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ iW.ker.comap (pullback.snd f f))
          (pullback.diagonal f ξ))) = 0 := by
    rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_sup_ker_stalkMap_diagonal f iV.ker iW.ker ξ]
    exact hcomponent
  have hpos := Stacks.Intersection.localIntersectionMultiplicity_pos_of_isRegularSequence
    g (RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom)
    (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
      (iV.ker.comap (pullback.fst f f) ⊔ iW.ker.comap (pullback.snd f f))
      (pullback.diagonal f ξ)) hgreg hgspan.symm h0
    (ringKrullDim_stalk_le_add_of_properIntersection_diagonal f iV iW ζ hproper)
  rw [Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity_eq,
    ← localIntersectionMultiplicity_stalk_comap_diagonal_eq k f iV.ker iW.ker ξ]
  exact hpos

end Geometric

end Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal

end
